title: $:/plugins/tiddlywiki/prosemirror/development

! ProseMirror plugin development

!! Design constraints

The saved value is WikiText, but the live editing state is a ProseMirror document. They are different coordinate systems. Editor actions must operate on the ProseMirror selection and transaction model; a ProseMirror position must never be used as a character offset into the saved WikiText.

The conversion layer preserves exact source for unchanged parse-tree groups. Unsupported inline and block syntax is represented by source-backed opaque nodes. New, duplicated or moved structure must have source-provenance attributes removed so serialisation reflects the new document order rather than stale input slices.

Interactive opaque nodes run with a block-local temporary `currentTiddler`. Third-party rule writes are bridged back through a ProseMirror transaction; do not render a stored parse tree with document-global source offsets or allow a node view to edit the canonical tiddler directly.

The standard toolbar and command menus are entry points, not mutation implementations. Toolbar messages are adapted by `core/text-operations.js`; `$:/tags/EditorCommand` descriptors used by slash and block surfaces are executed by `core/editor-commands.js`.

Every editor and node view uses its instance `ownerDocument`. Features that add DOM outside the editor or register listeners must clean them up in `destroy()`.

!! Vendored dependencies

Runtime ProseMirror packages are checked in under `files/` because browser editions cannot depend on a Node package installation. `vendor-manifest.json` records the exact package version, source file and SHA-256 digest for every artifact; `files/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES` contains the corresponding licences.

Use:

```
node bin/prosemirror-vendor.js --verify
```

to verify checked-in hashes without network access, and:

```
node bin/prosemirror-vendor.js --check
```

to install the exact versions in an isolated temporary directory and compare them byte for byte. Maintainers can use `--write` after intentionally changing the manifest versions.

Do not replace exact versions with `latest` URLs or manually edit vendored artifacts.

!! Layout

* `core/` — schema, engine, keymaps, toolbar adapter, semantic command execution and plugin assembly
* `ast/` — parse-tree conversion, WikiText serialisation and source provenance
* `blocks/` — specialised and source-backed node views
* `features/` — autocomplete, drag handle, find/replace, link tooltip, placeholders, Markdown-style input and slash menu
* `editor-actions/` — declarative command descriptors for command surfaces
* `tests/` — Jasmine unit and integration specifications
* `vendor-manifest.json` and `files/` — reproducible third-party runtime bundle

The reusable descriptor registry and DOM menu are in the separate `$:/plugins/tiddlywiki/editor-command-menu` plugin so they contain no ProseMirror, slash-trigger or block-handle policy.

!! Verification

Run the complete Node test edition:

```
npm test
```

For a quicker focused run after the test edition has been bootstrapped:

```
node editions/test/quick-test.js prosemirror editor-command-menu
```

Build the browser test edition before Playwright tests:

```
npm test
npx playwright test editions/test/prosemirror-playwright.spec.js --project=chromium --workers=1
```

The generated single-file test wiki is large, so using one worker also avoids loading several complete copies in parallel on development machines. The repository CI configuration already uses one worker.

Run lint and reproducibility checks before submitting:

```
npm run lint
node bin/prosemirror-vendor.js --verify
node bin/prosemirror-vendor.js --check
```
